<UserControl x:Class="SecureAD.Shell.Views.SettingsView" x:ClassModifier="internal"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
        Settings. What this installation has been told.

        EVERY SENTENCE HERE COMES FROM THE VIEW MODEL, and that is not house style for its own sake.
        The same number is stated in three places - this screen, the command line's help, and the
        sentence the new-audit review shows - and all three were approved together on 2026-09-13 so
        they could not drift into describing the number differently. A string typed into this file is
        a string no test can read, and the first one to be reworded here would be the one that
        disagrees.

        THE CONCURRENCY SETTING MUST NOT IMPLY that lowering the number is considerate. It
        governs this machine's disk and never a customer's domain controller; 0041 refused a lever
        over somebody else's server and still refuses one. A capture read more slowly is not a
        capture read more gently, and the wording says so outright rather than leaving an
        administrator to assume the kinder-sounding reading.

        THE RUN LIBRARY IS NOT HERE. It is chosen on Home, where an operator meets the question at
        the moment it matters. A second chooser over one value is how two controls come to disagree.
    -->

    <Grid Margin="{StaticResource ScreenPadding}">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Text="Settings"
                   Style="{StaticResource ScreenTitle}"
                   Margin="0,0,0,16" />

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" MaxWidth="640" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ConcurrencyHeading, Mode=OneTime}"
                           Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}"
                           Margin="0,0,0,8" />

                <TextBlock Text="{Binding WhatItIs, Mode=OneTime}"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Margin="0,0,0,10" />

                <!-- The paragraph carrying the whole distinction: whose machine is governed. -->
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding WhoseMachineItGoverns, Mode=OneTime}"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Margin="0,0,0,10" />

                <TextBlock Text="{Binding WhatLoweringItCosts, Mode=OneTime}"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource SecondaryTextBrush}"
                           Margin="0,0,0,14" />

                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                    <!-- Typed rather than stepped. A spinner cannot say why it refused, and the
                         two mistakes available here - a value that is not a number, and one below
                         one - deserve different sentences. Nothing is stored until it is
                         understood; see SettingsViewModel.Save. -->
                    <TextBox Text="{Binding Typed, UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}"
                             Width="80"
                             VerticalAlignment="Center" />

                    <Button Content="Save"
                            Command="{Binding SaveCommand}"
                            Margin="10,0,0,0" />
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- Amber, not red. 0056 decision 5 reserves red for critical findings and 0070
                     spends it only on a control that stops something running. A number this screen
                     would not accept is neither. -->
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Problem}"
                           Tag="Fault"
                           Style="{StaticResource StateText}"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Margin="0,10,0,0"
                           Visibility="{Binding HasProblem, Converter={StaticResource Shown}}" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>
        <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}" Margin="0,12,0,0">
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding AppearanceHeading,Mode=OneTime}"
                           Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,8" />
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding AppearanceExplanation,Mode=OneTime}"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,12" />
                <ComboBox Width="160" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                          ItemsSource="{Binding AppearanceChoices}"
                          SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedAppearance,Mode=TwoWay}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding AppearanceProblem}" Tag="Fault"
                           Style="{StaticResource StateText}" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           Margin="0,10,0,0"
                           Visibility="{Binding HasAppearanceProblem,Converter={StaticResource Shown}}" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
